Looking at this problem, I need to find the minimum number of ways (over all valid $n$) that $n$ can be written as a difference of two squares, given only that $k(n) = k \ge 2$.

**Answer Leak Check:** The problem text contains no leaked solutions or answer values. Proceeding.

